# Deafening Silence: each player can't cast more than one noncreature spell each turn; creature spells are not counted.
# Bot1 turn 1: Mox Pearl (noncreature, cast before Silence is out), then Deafening Silence itself (allowed: nothing
# limited it when it was cast) - but now a second Deafening Silence is refused with white mana ready (ruling: it looks at
# the whole turn, so you can't cast Silence and then another noncreature spell), while Thraben Inspector is cast after
# it. Bot2's turn 2: Mox Pearl, then Deafening Silence refused with white ready (each player). Turn 3, Bot1's: its second
# Silence is its first noncreature spell that turn, and Bot2, who has cast none this turn, answers with Swords to
# Plowshares (each player's count is its own). Turn 4, Bot2's: a creature first, then Deafening Silence (creature spells
# are not counted), and a second one is refused. CR 101.2, 601.3.

